     1	# Relux Proxy v0.2.0
     2	
     3	Relux Proxy v0.2.0 adds saved, independently controlled SSH SOCKS profiles to
     4	the native macOS menu-bar app.
     5	
     6	## Highlights
     7	
     8	- Save multiple profiles with stable identity and a unique local port.
     9	- Connect multiple profiles at once as concurrent local SOCKS endpoints on
    10	  `127.0.0.1`.
    11	- Use an IP address, DNS hostname, or SSH config alias without Relux Proxy
    12	  parsing or rewriting `~/.ssh/config`.
    13	- Leave Account empty to preserve the `User` selected by OpenSSH for a matching
    14	  SSH config alias, or set Account to pass an explicit `-l` user override.
    15	- Start, stop, diagnose, edit, and remove profiles independently. A failed or
    16	  occupied port affects only that profile.
    17	- Migrate the previous single-tunnel preferences once while retaining the old
    18	  keys for rollback compatibility.
    19	
    20	Relux Proxy continues to launch the system `/usr/bin/ssh` client. Each endpoint
    21	is an application SOCKS5 proxy for TCP traffic, not a system VPN. SOCKS-aware
    22	clients should enable SOCKS5h or proxy DNS when the remote SSH host must resolve
    23	private names.
    24	
    25	## Assets
    26	
    27	- `ReluxProxy-v0.2.0-universal.dmg` — versioned Apple silicon and Intel build.
    28	- `ReluxProxy.dmg` — stable-name copy of the same notarized DMG.
    29	- `SHA256SUMS` — SHA-256 hashes for both DMG names.
    30	
    31	The production GitLab pipeline publishes these assets only after verifying the
    32	accepted source commit, Relux GitLab project identity, Developer ID signature,
    33	universal architectures, Apple notarization ticket, stapling, Gatekeeper
    34	assessment, and checksums.

