     1	# Current state and future VPN boundary
     2	
     3	Last verified: 2026-07-28.
     4	
     5	## What exists
     6	
     7	The repository builds one SwiftPM macOS 14 executable, `ReluxProxy`, packaged by
     8	shell scripts as a menu bar `.app` and DMG.
     9	
    10	The app:
    11	
    12	- stores an ordered collection of profiles as one schema-versioned JSON Data
    13	  value under `legacySocksProfiles.v1`, with stable UUID identity and unique
    14	  explicit local ports;
    15	- migrates the legacy `sshHost`, `sshAccount`, and `localPort` values exactly
    16	  once, leaves those keys untouched for rollback, and never resurrects deleted
    17	  profiles after the migration marker is set;
    18	- owns one independent runtime session per profile, allowing multiple SSH
    19	  children and SOCKS tunnels to connect concurrently on different local ports;
    20	- launches `/usr/bin/ssh -N -C -D 127.0.0.1:<port>` with fail-fast, keepalive,
    21	  timeout, batch-mode, and quiet logging options;
    22	- passes an empty account as the bare host target, allowing system OpenSSH to
    23	  use a matching `User` setting (or its normal default); a non-empty account is
    24	  sent with `-l account` while the destination remains the bare host or alias,
    25	  which explicitly overrides only the SSH user;
    26	- accepts an IP address, hostname, or `Host` alias and lets the system client
    27	  apply matching `~/.ssh/config` behavior such as `HostName`, `Port`,
    28	  `IdentityFile`, and `ProxyJump`;
    29	- binds the SOCKS listener only to IPv4 loopback (`127.0.0.1`) and keeps a
    30	  separate trailing 4,000-character in-memory diagnostic for every session;
    31	- rejects duplicate saved ports and externally occupied loopback ports without
    32	  stopping or modifying another session or process;
    33	- reports connecting, connected, disconnecting, disconnected, and failed states
    34	  per row, with aggregate menu-bar status;
    35	- prevents profile edits and removal while that profile owns a starting,
    36	  connected, or stopping child;
    37	- stops every child it owns on normal quit and starts every saved profile
    38	  disconnected on the next launch, with no automatic retry or reconnect;
    39	- exposes every listed endpoint as an Application SOCKS5 proxy — TCP only; not
    40	  a system VPN or system-wide routing. Users configure a SOCKS-aware client
    41	  manually and enable proxy DNS/SOCKS5h when private names need the remote
    42	  resolver;
    43	- intentionally runs outside the App Sandbox so it can spawn system SSH.
    44	
    45	Tests cover profile migration and persistence, command construction and account
    46	precedence, duplicate and OS port conflicts, concurrent independent lifecycle,
    47	stale callback protection, diagnostics, active mutation rejection, and
    48	coordinated shutdown. CI runs `swift test` and builds an ad-hoc-signed universal
    49	application bundle.
    50	
    51	The v0.2.0 release automation imports the Relux Works Developer ID certificate
    52	into a disposable keychain, builds a universal app, signs the DMG, notarizes and
    53	staples it, validates it with Gatekeeper, publishes checksums, and verifies both
    54	the versioned and stable `ReluxProxy.dmg` GitLab Release assets. It refuses the
    55	wrong host, project, accepted commit, runner, identity, or unsigned fallback.
    56	Production publication remains externally blocked until the exact Relux GitLab
    57	project, authorization, protected macOS runner, and notarization variables are
    58	confirmed; no GitLab v0.2.0 release is currently claimed.
    59	
    60	## What does not exist
    61	
    62	The current app is not a system VPN and does not contain:
    63	
    64	- iOS targets;
    65	- `NETunnelProviderManager` or packet-tunnel extensions;
    66	- a userspace TCP/IP stack or packetFlow bridge;
    67	- an embedded SSH implementation;
    68	- UDP or system DNS forwarding;
    69	- the remote `relux-relay` executable/protocol;
    70	- shared profile/Keychain state between host and extension;
    71	- Network Extension entitlements or provisioning;
    72	- TestFlight/App Store release automation.
    73	
    74	## Implemented legacy migration
    75	
    76	The [multi-profile usage guide](../README.md#use) describes the user-facing
    77	workflow. The implementation above provides the one-time migration, profile
    78	persistence, OpenSSH account precedence, port ownership, diagnostics, and
    79	independent lifecycle. Runtime state and reconnect intent are never persisted.
    80	
    81	The [remote VPN reachability guide](socks-vpn-reachability.md) documents the
    82	same application-level boundary, proxy-side DNS, and redacted diagnostics. A
    83	remote VPN route, the authenticated `sshd` forwarding process/account policy,
    84	and the remote firewall must all permit the requested TCP destination; Relux
    85	Proxy does not change local system proxy, DNS, or routes.
    86	
    87	The planned VPN product in `.spec/` remains a new architecture, not an
    88	incremental toggle inside the legacy SOCKS controller.
    89	
    90	For future VPN work:
    91	
    92	- the stable macOS release path must remain reproducible;
    93	- any migration from legacy SOCKS profiles to VPN profiles still needs its own
    94	  explicit product decision;
    95	- the system-SSH implementation may remain as a macOS legacy mode, be replaced,
    96	  or be retired only through a product decision;
    97	- SwiftPM tests and release history must not be silently discarded;
    98	- Network Extension code must not be backported into the current manual app
    99	  without the architecture and entitlement gates in `.spec/validation.md`.

